  "candidate_A_within_process_bit_deterministic": false,
  "candidate_B_within_process_repeats_differ_at_1e-4": true,
  "supported": "B",
  "evidence": "Within a single process the same state re-evaluated by the same path is NOT bit-reproducible: 5 hook repeats on the reverse-splice state gave 5 distinct bit patterns in each process (spreads 1.98e-4 and 3.66e-4), and 5 per-item repeats likewise (2.75e-4 and 7.02e-4).  Over the 10 values of a process-state block, 9/10, 9/10, 10/10 and 10/10 bit patterns were distinct.  So the 07:56 equality is NOT the expected behaviour of a deterministic pair of paths and is recorded as UNEXPLAINED.",
  "what_the_data_also_show_about_the_ulp_argument": "The relevant resolution is not the float64 ulp (4.5e-13).  All observed values lie on a coarse lattice: on the reverse-splice state the step is 2**-16 = 1.52587890625e-05 for both paths (the per-item losses are float32 .item() values at that magnitude), and the whole observed spread is only ~25-46 steps wide; on the baseline-B state the step is 2**-21 = 4.76837158203125e-07 and the spread ~138-149 steps.  Exact equalities therefore do occur and were directly observed here.  Within a process: 2 identical pairs over the 4 state-blocks of 45 unordered pairs each = 2/180 (process 1 reverse state, one hook == one per-item mean, 3173.6402893066406; process 1 baseline, two per-item repeats equal, 1144.636215209961).  Pooling both processes: on the reverse-splice state 4 identical pairs of 190 (2.1 %), of which 3 of the 100 cross-process pairs; on the baseline state 1 of 190 (0.5 %), none cross-process.  These are measured rates, stated as rates; they are not offered as an explanation of the 07:56 value.",
  "what_is_NOT_claimed": "The 07:56 equality is not called a coincidence, and no mechanism is asserted for it.  It stands as an unexplained exact equality between two independently computed values in a pipeline that is measurably non-reproducible at ~1e-4."
 },
 "clamp_probe_note": "Both processes end with a direct check of the clamp finding behind extra5: edges_syn_strength.requires_grad is True, a -0.5 written into T2 synapse slot 2 reads back as exactly 0.0 after a single hook_eval, i.e. Network.forward() clamps in place at evaluation time.  This contradicts splice_a.py:232-236 and README 'Network.clamp() ... is called in training only'."
